{"schemaVersion":1,"systemCode":"BSI:ell-Grek:Latn:1958","dependencies":[],"metadata":{"authority_id":"bsi","id":"1958","language":"iso-639-2:ell","source_script":"Grek","destination_script":"Latn","name":"BS 2979:1958 Transliteration of Cyrillic and Greek characters - Table G, Transliteration of Greek characters","url":"https://www.bsigroup.com","creation_date":"1958","confirmation_date":"2000-05","description":"BS 2979:1958, Table G: a letter-for-letter system for Greek, aimed at\n    cataloguers and providing a one-to-one correspondence between Greek and\n    Roman characters in both directions.","notes":["Special signs (a): the rough breathing sign is transliterated by the comma, or by an apostrophe over the preceding initial vowel or diphthong (e.g. 'E, 'Ou); over rho it is disregarded. This map renders the rough breathing as the apostrophe preceding its vowel, and deletes it over rho.","Special signs (b): the smooth breathing sign is not transliterated; its presence in Greek is implied where the rough breathing sign is considered to be part of the transliterated text. This map deletes the smooth breathing sign.","Special signs (c): a diaeresis in the original Greek text is always reproduced in the transliterated text; this map leaves diaeresis marks in place.","Special signs (d): the acute, grave and circumflex accent signs may, also, if desired, be rendered as in the Greek; this map leaves accent marks in place.","Special signs (e): iota subscript, even when adscripted (a subscript in capitalized Greek texts), is always rendered by positional i (small); this map renders the iota subscript sign as i following its vowel.","The numerical values of the ancient Greek characters run parallel with the Church Slavonic Cyrillic (Table D), distinguished up to 999 by a postliteral sign above the line and from 1000 onwards by a preliteral sign below the line; this map renders letters, not numeral values.","The English-to-Greek column notes that Ch, ch is rendered via eta (see H) and Kh, kh likewise; Ph, ph is rendered via phi (see F), which this table romanizes f.","Transcribed visually from the scanned table pages of the digitized BS 2979:1958 (BSI 05-2000 reprint); the source's own text layer for this table stores the Greek letters in a legacy 8-bit font and was not used."]},"stages":[{"kind":"stage","name":"main","rules":[{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"ρ"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"r"},"after":{"kind":"string","value":"̔"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"Ρ"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"R"},"after":{"kind":"string","value":"̔"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"Α"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"’Α"},"after":{"kind":"string","value":"̔"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"α"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"’α"},"after":{"kind":"string","value":"̔"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"Ε"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"’Ε"},"after":{"kind":"string","value":"̔"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"ε"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"’ε"},"after":{"kind":"string","value":"̔"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"Η"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"’Η"},"after":{"kind":"string","value":"̔"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"η"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"’η"},"after":{"kind":"string","value":"̔"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"Ι"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"’Ι"},"after":{"kind":"string","value":"̔"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"ι"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"’ι"},"after":{"kind":"string","value":"̔"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"Ο"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"’Ο"},"after":{"kind":"string","value":"̔"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"ο"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"’ο"},"after":{"kind":"string","value":"̔"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"Υ"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"’Υ"},"after":{"kind":"string","value":"̔"}},{"